    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i look at my dad and my brother and i just see the same patterns. it’s like it’s all pre-written in the dna or something. no matter how much i try to stay positive or do the therapy stuff, i can feel it just waiting for me. like i’m just a passenger in a body that's eventually gonna break. it feels so useless to even fight it.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It can be incredibly frustrating and disempowering to feel like patterns of behavior are determined by genetics. This realization can also raise questions about the nature of free will and personal agency. It's possible that you're experiencing a sense of emotional resonance or shared patterns within your family, rather than a literal genetic programming. Acknowledging and exploring these feelings can be a powerful step towards understanding and breaking patterns.",
      "source": "target",
